            <creation xml:id="creation_id6cdf8390">
               <date isodate="1848" xml:id="date_b2b33118">1848</date>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_idfe098473">
               <p xml:id="idm110">The piece was presumably inspired by Hartmann's visit in the summer of 1848 to the manor Tiselholt on Funen which had belonged to his deceased farther-in-law. Here he had met a group of Swedish officers who were housed at Tiselholt. Later the owner of the estate, Carl Ulrich Jørgensen, sent a copy of "Svensk Hjemvee" to one of these officers, as his adjutant was the Swedish pianist and composer Ludvig Leonard Löwegren (1817-1894).</p>
            </history>
